// Codex 5: the people. Every human identity in the computer, two entries
// a person where the Character Sheet gives enough: the first is what they
// might tell a stranger, the second is what has to be forced out of them.
//
// Performers' entries are `about:` the performer, so each performer holds
// their own from the start. Featured entries are `about:` the featured
// CHARACTER (harmless: the guest who plays that program receives them in
// `Featured Briefing`). The four Antivirus entries carry codes: their
// personnel files are hidden around the house for Bugdom to find.
// Everyone receives every entry at the end (the recount, truth.txt).
//
// Every person's last entry ends with "Why Trabolta chose you", because
// truth.txt and the recount must say why each person was brought in.
//
// Rules for this file: no actor names (only the in-fiction ones the
// Character Sheet gives), no line may start with a program's name and a
// colon, and nothing here mentions Sandy or the server room (a performer's
// codex rides along when they talk to Trabolta).

// ── Hosts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX The Clinic
  title: The Clinic
  about: Clippy
  text:
    Before the computer, Clippy spent her first five years out of
    veterinary school at a desperately underfunded nonprofit veterinary
    clinic. She believed she was helping animals every single day. She
    still talks about the animals.

CODEX Saline
  title: Saline
  about: Clippy
  text:
    The clinic was totally unlicensed. It was not a nonprofit, and it was
    not a veterinary clinic. It was a front for everything possible, and
    for five years she was only ever injecting the animals with saline.
    The fake vet promised to pay off her student debt and disappeared. She
    was left with no faith in humanity, no relevant job experience, and a
    lot of debt. Then a letter arrived promising a new community game
    night where she could truly help people all night, as an organiser of
    fun philanthropy party games that would help research towards ending
    all of the world's problems, and debt would no longer be relevant.
    Why Trabolta chose you: you were the perfect traumatised cult servant
    who desperately needs to rebuild an identity. He promised you could
    help people all night, and that your debt would no longer be relevant.

CODEX Middle Management
  title: Middle Management
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Task Manager was a middle manager in IT at Urban Outfitters. He has no
    real idiosyncrasies and no personality to speak of: a drone bee,
    programmed only to be a milquetoast middle manager. He manages tasks.

CODEX Replaced By Clippy
  title: Replaced By Clippy
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Senior management let him go when they realised he could be replaced
    with an AI Clippy. With no goals left in sight, he was totally
    aimless. Now he keeps things running for the very assistant that took
    his job, and he has not said a word about it.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he wanted someone in the computer who would be
    totally bereft of political motivation, who would simply follow
    instructions and manage tasks without any controversy or ever drawing
    too much attention.

CODEX Sheryl Terrio
  title: Sheryl Terrio
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    Adobe Acrobat is Sheryl Terrio, the world's most successful
    motivational speaker. She reached great wealth through online
    self-mastery courses. Her presence is so motivational that her paid
    clients reached their full potential almost at once, and never needed
    to pay her another cent.

CODEX The Pirated Masterclass
  title: The Pirated Masterclass
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    When her Masterclass was pirated, her profits fell through: anyone who
    saw a single clip was instantly so motivated that they did not need to
    pay her for anything. She is still seeking new ways to prove she is a
    master, and she is frustrated with never being paid for it.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he recruited you for a paid motivational guest
    speaker role in a computer simulation, working with lots of people who
    are excited to create things, where you would be the paid bottleneck
    that enables their creativity, by pretending to be Adobe Acrobat.

CODEX The Attendant
  title: The Attendant
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    Recycling Bin was a bathroom attendant, laid off during COVID and
    never rehired. He had great potential in life for skilled work, but
    never believed he could rise above encouraging men in the bathroom to
    groom themselves better.

CODEX The Oscars Of Bathrooms
  title: The Oscars Of Bathrooms
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    The invitation offered him the role of pretending to be a Recycling
    Bin at a computer-themed resort. For a bathroom attendant, this is the
    equivalent of getting to work the Oscars. He keeps Disk Cleanup
    spotless, and he is very proud of Bathroom Mode.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a computer-themed resort needs a Recycling
    Bin, and you had great potential for skilled work that you never
    believed you could reach.

// ── The Antivirus (personnel files, hidden around the house) ───────

CODEX Julie Norton
  title: Julie Norton
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  code: NORTON-RELAY
  text:
    PERSONNEL FILE. Norton Anti-Virus, real name Julie Norton, was a Red
    Bull Horse Relay Champion. In 2020 the COVID lockdowns took her trade,
    then her horses, then her family. Cut off from everything that gave
    her meaning, she became totally housebound with paranoia about
    viruses, and spent her days reporting pirated files being shared on
    Reddit.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a perfect enforcer, to be a moderator in a new
    digital chatroom in the Metaverse.

CODEX The Moderator
  title: The Moderator
  about: McAfee Anti-Virus
  code: MCAFEE-MOD
  text:
    PERSONNEL FILE. McAfee Anti-Virus was a Reddit moderator for
    /r/bitcoin who never invested in crypto, and feels real remorse over
    never earning anything from the investments they predicted, because
    they were too consumed with moderating the subreddit.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a decade of moderation experience. Your
    secret: you want a role of power and influence in the Metaverse, to
    exploit the exchange of information and become rich.

CODEX Yugi Moto
  title: Yugi Moto
  about: Password Manager
  code: YUGI-MOTO
  text:
    PERSONNEL FILE. Password Manager is a Yu-gi-oh! fanatic who changed
    her name to Yugi Moto. After a falling out with the team at the local
    Gamestop she looked for another club, and there were none in Halifax.
    She was kicked out of board game night at the Board Room Cafe. The
    Hells Angels rejected her for talking about Yu-gi-oh!. Religious
    organisations and Meetup.com groups kept throwing her out for the same
    reason. Rejection by the Waegwoltic Social Club was the last straw.
    Why Trabolta chose you: an experimental procedure, an eternal
    Metaverse simulation, and the job of managing all passwords and who
    gets to be part of what clubs (and of injecting Yu-gi-oh! where it
    does not belong).

CODEX One Cent On The Dollar
  title: One Cent On The Dollar
  about: CRA Agent Software
  code: CRA-PENNY
  text:
    PERSONNEL FILE. CRA Agent Software was an NSCC administrative
    assistant intern, left in charge of the entire finances of the City of
    Halifax under Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr. after the other staff quit in
    protest of the Data Centre. Barkmore Jr. encouraged her to stay by
    showing her how to siphon 0.01 cents off every dollar the City spent.
    She accidentally siphoned 1 cent off every dollar and was caught
    immediately. While the RCMP investigated, "Mark Carney" reached out to
    her personally with a deal: pay back the hundreds of thousands she
    took, or spend what will physically be one day, but feel like an
    eternity, inside an experimental digital Canada. Mark Carney was
    Trabolta.
    Why Trabolta chose you: the other staff quit and you were left with
    the City's finances. He wants your financial expertise, as a digital
    CRA Agent, for one day that feels like eternity.

// ── WebMD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INVENTED: the Character Sheet gives WebMD no backstory. This one is
// new for the rewrite and is flagged for review (design spec §10.1).

CODEX The Symptom Checker
  title: The Symptom Checker
  about: WebMD
  text:
    Before the computer, WebMD ran an online symptom checker that
    diagnosed every single user with everything. A headache? Everything.
    A sore knee? Everything. The lawsuits came in alphabetical order. The
    invitation offered a wellness role "where nobody can sue."
    Why Trabolta chose you: a wellness voice nobody can sue, to keep the
    re-education gentle.

// ── The featured programs (guests with written characters) ─────────

CODEX Randy Barkmore Sr
  title: Randy Barkmore Sr.
  about: Microsoft Excel
  text:
    In reality, Microsoft Excel is the ninety-year-old former Mayor of
    Halifax, Randy Barkmore Sr. His son, Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr., died in
    a sinkhole at the opening of Halifax's first AI Data Centre, built on
    the site of the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery. He arrived
    five hours early, at 4 a.m., because he was so excited. Randy Sr.
    became seriously concerned for the family legacy and needed more time
    on this earth, so he could run for Mayor one more time. The invitation
    offered a pilot program for uploading your consciousness to the Cloud,
    promising everlasting life.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he knew you would say yes to everlasting life,
    and he wants you here to persuade all of the other programs that they
    should remain.

CODEX Dana Anderson
  title: Dana Anderson
  about: OpenOffice
  text:
    OpenOffice, in reality, is Dana Anderson: a former FBI agent turned
    independent hacker, who regretted her role in a sting of a landlord in
    Halifax nine years ago, and turned to trying to make all information
    free. A conflicted rebel with incredible fact-finding skills, she was
    deeply opposed to the authoritarian steamrolling of the Data Centre
    that nobody in Halifax wanted, and used old FBI tactics to sabotage the
    construction site, with a planned destruction for the early morning
    before the official opening. On opening day, Randy Barkmore Jr.
    arrived five hours early, at 4 a.m., because he was so excited. The
    Data Centre was destroyed on schedule. She lives with extreme guilt
    and paranoia.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he believes you want a chance at a new life in
    the cloud, and he wants your investigative skills. You will be the
    leader of the "get out of the computer" faction.

CODEX The Paperclip Trade
  title: The Paperclip Trade
  about: DraftKings
  text:
    In real life, DraftKings was a degenerate gambler who traded a
    paperclip for a quarter, put the quarter in a slot machine and got a
    dollar, then played progressive blackjack until they literally won
    Casino Nova Scotia. Then they gambled Casino Nova Scotia on other
    casinos, and won most of the casinos in Atlantic Canada.

CODEX The Boardwalk Bet
  title: The Boardwalk Bet
  about: DraftKings
  text:
    Obsessed with Monopoly, DraftKings went all in: the entire casino
    chain, against a block of properties in downtown Halifax, especially
    the Boardwalk, in a game of online poker. They lost. They did not know
    their opponent was Trabolta, who had already taken the Maps And Ducks
    building by citing ownership of the website as ownership of the
    business.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he needed someone powerful with numbers on its
    side. If you live here, you can gamble forever, and win unimaginably
    big sums.

CODEX Bugdom VR
  title: Bugdom VR
  about: Bugdom
  text:
    In real life, Bugdom worked an unhappy pet-store job, selling crickets
    and ants, and always had the fantasy of living inside an extremely
    expansive VR version of the old game Bugdom. Every day they rushed home
    to an old laptop to keep designing concept assets for Bugdom VR. That
    is how they spent the last ten years.

CODEX The Fire Ants
  title: The Fire Ants
  about: Bugdom
  text:
    One day, fire ants that had gotten loose in their work lunchbox
    crawled inside the laptop that held the only copy of the Bugdom VR
    assets. All the work was permanently lost. Bugdom fell into a
    catatonic panic, manically writing down everything they had done so
    far, to dedicate the rest of their life to rebuilding it.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he promised a VR world with unlimited Bugdom
    right away. Really, he wants the use of your relentless pursuit of
    tedious tasks.

CODEX The Valley Librarian
  title: The Valley Librarian
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  text:
    In real life, Broken Ask Jeeves was a talented and helpful youth
    librarian in the Annapolis Valley library system, until government
    cuts made the position redundant and left them without purpose. They
    thought tonight was a job interview, for a digital librarian in the
    Metaverse.

CODEX The DSL Line
  title: The DSL Line
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  text:
    The transmission into the computer happened over a malfunctioning DSL
    line on the old Valley infrastructure. The download missed some files,
    and this Ask Jeeves Desktop Helper now malfunctions occasionally, or
    behaves completely erratically.
    Why Trabolta chose you: to sort all the unorganised information in the
    computer. He did not foresee the upload going badly.

CODEX Twenty Four Years Online
  title: Twenty Four Years Online
  about: Runescape
  text:
    In real life, Runescape is a 34-year-old who played Runescape every
    day for 24 years and became the richest and most powerful player in
    the world. That took a PhD in economics at the Wharton School, where
    she became a staunch libertarian and decided her life's mission is to
    convert every modern economy back to the gold standard, like they have
    in Runescape. The invitation offered her a job as economy consultant
    for a new MMORPG said to be even more interactive than Runescape.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he needs you to understand the market
    incentives of everyone's behaviour, to serve his need to exchange
    information and get all the facts.

CODEX Expelled From NSCAD
  title: Expelled From NSCAD
  about: MS Paint
  text:
    MS Paint was an art student kicked out of NSCAD for a staunch refusal
    to work in any artistic medium other than MS Paint for her degree in
    digital art. Her position: "any program that relies on algorithms is
    a betrayal of the artist." She came because she thought she was being
    paid to teach an online MS Paint art class inside the Metaverse. She
    realised at once how limiting this place is, and she wants out.
    Why Trabolta chose you: he believes having an artist on site will help
    improve the overall vibes and morale within the computer.

CODEX Victor Louis Christianson
  title: Victor Louis Christianson
  about: VLC
  text:
    VLC is a failed looksmaxxing influencer, birth name Victor Louis
    Christianson. He had millions of followers on his VLC The Playa
    channel, until a livestream fail: he sneezed too early after a Turkish
    face tightening, his whole face fell right off, and his followers went
    to zero on the spot.
    Why Trabolta chose you: you would want to stay in a computer and keep
    your beauty forever, and he wants your charisma and influencer powers
    to convince everyone to help him.

// INVENTED: the Character Sheet gives no reason for Pong; the "why" line
// is new for the rewrite (design spec §10.1).
CODEX Tennis For Two
  title: Tennis For Two
  about: Pong
  text:
    Pong is the child of William Higinbotham, who built Tennis For Two,
    the first video game, at Brookhaven in 1958. The invitation asked them
    to present a seminar on the importance of nuclear non-proliferation,
    under the guise of everyone in the Metaverse getting to play a fun
    game of Pong.
    Why Trabolta chose you: a mind that knows how to stop an arms race, in
    case the programs start one.
